From 1600d91071cf97307924d4b1c85482b4d894eef9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anonymous <anonymous@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 01:03:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat: detector 5 external testbed on MIMIC-IV and eICU demo

Implements the pre-registered variants and cases. The diagnostic itself
is split into run_check_on_stays so external data runs the SAME code as
PhysioNet rather than a reimplementation, which would validate the
rewrite instead of the detector.

Two constraints the external path must respect: read raw_ts, never
sample["values"], because the processed values are MinMax-normalized and
forward-filled and both would destroy the signal; and the oxygen term is
the Severinghaus relation rather than PhysioNet's O2Sat-vs-SaO2 pair,
since the demo datasets record no SaO2. The external component set is
analogous, not identical.

Ground truth is controlled ablation: observations are deleted, the
surviving values are untouched, so physiology is fixed and only recording
availability moves.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
